  "visual_findings": [
    "Hand A was tested at one additional inward yaw level. After the support preparation, servo 1 revisited 1577 us (reference +40), then separately reached 1617 us (+80), returned through +40 and zero, and the support returned. Servo 2 pitch, servo 3 head yaw and hand B were fixed. All six edges had paired camera reviews.",
    "The extra +40 edge visibly moved the hand/rod/body system further inward, but also increased torso turning and changed the body projection. This is not an independently verified hand crossing or a calibrated torso-relative endpoint.",
    "Returning from +80 to +40 and to zero produced visible recovery. Exact wrist coordinates, joint angles, millimetre clearance and repeatability tolerances were not measured. No further inward amplitude or head-top movement was attempted.",
    "No obvious rod interference, detached rod or curtain exit was visible in the reviewed images. This is not a force measurement. The other hand and tiger were not tested in this route; all tiger outputs remained disabled.",
    "The fixed closed command route ended normally with all ten PWM outputs off at sequence 3658. The original incident locks were retained. No automatic replay or full crossing was validated."
